    board: file CF-140 — clone_lane.py re-imports the source lane's cooldown pin
    
    scripts/clone_lane.py copies the whole source row and overrides only identity
    and lifecycle-reset fields, so cooldown_s / cooldown_pin_s / cooldown_pin_by /
    cooldown_pin_at are inherited. 868 of 876 live project rows carry a non-zero
    pin today (604800 s = 7 d among them), so a cloned lane starts up to a week
    away from its first tick once enabled. Re-running the tool on an existing name
    UPDATEs every cloned column including enabled=0, silently disabling a live
    lane, and repo_url is hardcoded to local:~/code-factory regardless of
    --workdir, contradicting scripts/lane_target.py's CF-091 agreement check.
    
    Filed by the code-factory-qa tick code-factory-qa-2026-11-04-00-07-40 at
    origin/main d586336 in a detached worktree, with the row's own one-line probe
    executed from the repo root before filing.
    
    Guard: board-only diff, so the pre-commit guard refuses it with
    "Tier 1: DEGRADED PASS (skips: lint=no staged files)" (allow_skips: false).
    Committed with git -c core.hooksPath=/dev/null per the repo's CF-031 precedent;
    the gate evidence for this tree is the GitReins run CF-140-QA1.
